  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Looping over all childs of a transform to find a certain child with a given name is really expensive in Udon. It's what takes one of the biggest performance hits currently in our scripts. You cannot use Transform.Find() in a lot of cases which is the closest Unity function to that.\nI noticed that having a native function from VRChat doing this for us would be a good way to increase performance, especially if this search is also done over childs of childs etc., while it's also easily to implement.\nIdeally, we would get a GetChildWithName() function that returns the child which has a name that starts with a given string (so instead of String.Equals it uses String.StartsWith()), plus the optional parameter if disabled gameObjects should be included or not, and an optional parameter if this search should only be performed for direct childs or also for childs of childs (all layers down). Furthermore, a function that returns an array of all findings would be great. These functions could be added to the Utilities class for example. \nNote: Transform.Find(), which is the closest Unity function to this, does not perform a recursive descend down a Transform hierarchy, so it does not cover this use case.",
